      "message": "In `mc_AddCustomPythonHooks`, the `try...except` Exception: blocks are very broad. This will catch any error, potentially masking issues beyond a symbol not being found. If the only expected error is the symbol not existing, it would be better to catch a more specific exception if the Renode API provides one. At a minimum, consider logging a warning when a symbol is not found, e.g.:\n\n```\ntry:\n    results \u003d cpu.Bus.GetAllSymbolAddresses(\"sx_hash_feed\")\n    if not results:\n        logging.warning(\"Symbol not found: sx_hash_feed\")\n    for addr in results:\n        cpu.AddHook(addr, sx_hash_hooks.hook_feed)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    logging.error(f\"Error adding hook for sx_hash_feed: {e}\")\n```",
